        "document_content": "Open Access populations. Overall FCI was associated with lower post­ natal mortality among live-born infants without a signifi­ cant difference in live birth. The most consistent signals were observed for lower postnatal death among live-born infants after FAV and for improved BVC and live birth after technically successful FAV, whereas FPV and FASI remained less certain because of small numbers and end­ point-specific limitations. BVC is widely recognized as an indicator of favorable long-term prognosis, and individual studies have reported post-FAV BVC rates ranging from 40% to 74% [11, 16, 17, 20, 24-31]. Prior meta-analyses compared intervention and control groups drawn from different studies rather than",
